Joystick Controlled Pan-Tilt Servo System

A simple Arduino project that controls two servo motors using a joystick module.
The joystick provides two-axis control:

X-axis → controls horizontal servo movement
Y-axis → controls vertical servo movement

This creates a basic pan-tilt mechanism commonly used in robotics, camera mounts, and targeting systems.

Components Used
Arduino UNO
2 × SG90 Servo Motors
Joystick Module
Breadboard
Jumper Wires
Connections
Joystick Module
Joystick Pin	Arduino Pin
VRx	A0
VRy	A5
VCC	5V
GND	GND
Servo Motors
Servo	Signal Pin
Servo 1	D11
Servo 2	D9
Features
Dual-axis servo control
Real-time joystick movement
Smooth servo operation
Beginner-friendly robotics project
Simple hardware setup
Applications
Robotic pan-tilt systems
Camera positioning systems
Robotic arm control
Surveillance mechanisms
Motion control experiments
Future Improvements
Bluetooth control
Wireless joystick
LCD angle display
Camera mounting
Gyroscope stabilization
